---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import LocalBusinessSchema from "../../components/LocalBusinessSchema.astro";

---

<BaseLayout
  title="Emergency Tree Removal South Florida | 24/7 Storm Damage Response"
  description="24/7 emergency tree removal services in South Florida. Fast response for storm damage, fallen trees, and hazardous situations threatening homes and businesses."
  canonical="https://sftreeremoval.com/emergency-tree-removal/"
>
  <!-- ================= LOCAL BUSINESS SCHEMA ================= -->
  <LocalBusinessSchema />

  <!-- ================= HERO ================= -->
  <section class="bg-teal-900 py-28 text-white">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 text-center">

      <span
        class="inline-block mb-6 px-4 py-1 text-xs font-bold tracking-widest
               border border-dashed border-white/60 rounded-full"
      >
        24/7 EMERGENCY SERVICE
      </span>

      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl xl:text-6xl font-extrabold leading-tight">
        Emergency Tree Removal<br class="hidden sm:block" />
        in South Florida
      </h1>

      <p class="mt-8 max-w-3xl mx-auto text-lg text-white/90">
        Immediate response for storm damage, fallen trees, and hazardous
        situations threatening homes, businesses, and power lines across
        South Florida.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-12 flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-6">

        <a
          href="/contact-us/"
          class="inline-flex items-center gap-4 rounded-full
                 border border-white/70 px-10 py-4 text-white font-bold
                 hover:bg-white/10 transition"
        >
          Request Immediate Help
        </a>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

<!-- ================= COMMON EMERGENCY TREE SITUATIONS ================= -->
<section class="bg-[#f4f8f6] py-32">
  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6">

    <!-- HEADER -->
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto text-center mb-20">
      <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 mb-6">
        Common Emergency Tree Situations
      </h2>
      <p class="text-lg text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
        Emergency tree removal is required when damaged or unstable trees create
        immediate safety risks. Below are the most common situations that require
        urgent professional response.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- INCIDENT GRID -->
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-8">

      <!-- ITEM -->
      <div class="bg-white rounded-3xl p-8">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-extrabold text-slate-900 mb-3">
          Storm-Damaged or Fallen Trees
        </h3>
        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
          Trees that have fallen or sustained storm damage may block driveways,
          roads, or restrict access to homes and businesses, requiring immediate
          removal to restore safety and access.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- ITEM -->
      <div class="bg-white rounded-3xl p-8">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-extrabold text-slate-900 mb-3">
          Trees Leaning Toward Structures
        </h3>
        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
          After storms, flooding, or soil saturation, trees may begin leaning
          toward homes, buildings, or fences, increasing the risk of sudden
          collapse.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- ITEM -->
      <div class="bg-white rounded-3xl p-8">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-extrabold text-slate-900 mb-3">
          Broken or Hanging Limbs
        </h3>
        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
          Large broken limbs hanging over roofs, vehicles, or walkways pose an
          immediate danger to people and property and must be removed safely.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- ITEM -->
      <div class="bg-white rounded-3xl p-8">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-extrabold text-slate-900 mb-3">
          Trees Entangled with Power Lines
        </h3>
        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
          Trees in contact with power lines require controlled, professional
          removal to avoid electrocution, outages, and further infrastructure
          damage.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- ITEM (FULL WIDTH) -->
      <div class="bg-white rounded-3xl p-8 md:col-span-2">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-extrabold text-slate-900 mb-3">
          Uprooted or Structurally Unstable Trees
        </h3>
        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
          Trees with exposed or compromised root systems are at high risk of
          sudden collapse, especially during high winds or heavy rainfall,
          requiring immediate professional assessment and removal.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>

    <!-- CTA -->
    <div class="mt-20 text-center">
      <a
        href="/contact-us/"
        class="inline-flex items-center gap-4 rounded-full
               bg-teal-700 px-12 py-5 text-white font-extrabold
               hover:bg-teal-800 transition"
      >
        Request Emergency Service
        <span class="flex h-10 w-10 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-white/15">
          ↗
        </span>
      </a>

      <p class="mt-6 text-sm text-slate-500">
        Available 24/7 for emergency tree removal across South Florida
      </p>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>

<!-- ================= COMMON TREE EMERGENCY SITUATIONS ================= -->
<section class="bg-white py-32">
  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6">

    <!-- HEADER -->
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto text-center mb-16">
      <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 mb-6">
        Common Tree Emergency Situations
      </h2>
      <p class="text-lg text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
        Tree emergencies often occur without warning and require immediate,
        professional tree removal services. Below are the most common emergency
        situations we respond to across South Florida.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- CONTENT -->
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto space-y-8 text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">

      <p>
        <strong class="text-slate-900">
          Storm-damaged or fallen trees
        </strong>
        are one of the most frequent reasons for emergency tree removal.
        Hurricanes, tropical storms, and high winds can cause trees to fall
        across driveways, roads, or directly onto homes and commercial
        buildings, creating immediate safety hazards.
      </p>

      <p>
        <strong class="text-slate-900">
          Trees leaning after hurricanes or heavy rain
        </strong>
        often indicate compromised root systems caused by flooding or soil
        saturation. These trees may collapse suddenly and require urgent
        professional assessment and removal.
      </p>

      <p>
        <strong class="text-slate-900">
          Broken or hanging limbs
        </strong>
        pose a serious risk when suspended over roofs, vehicles, walkways, or
        public areas. Emergency tree service is necessary to safely remove these
        limbs before they fall and cause injury or property damage.
      </p>

      <p>
        <strong class="text-slate-900">
          Trees entangled with power lines
        </strong>
        require controlled emergency tree removal performed by experienced
        crews using specialized equipment. These situations are extremely
        dangerous and should never be handled without professional support.
      </p>

      <p>
        <strong class="text-slate-900">
          Uprooted or structurally unstable trees
        </strong>
        with exposed or weakened root systems are at high risk of sudden
        collapse, especially during additional storms or high winds. Immediate
        action helps prevent further damage and ensures public safety.
      </p>

    </div>

  </div>
</section>

<!-- ================= EMERGENCY RESPONSE PROCESS ================= -->
<section
  class="relative py-32 bg-fixed bg-center bg-cover"
  style="background-image:url('/images/emergency-tree-removal/emergency-response-process.jpg')"
>
  <!-- OVERLAY -->
  <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-teal-900/70"></div>

  <div class="relative z-10 max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 text-white">

    <!-- HEADER -->
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto text-center mb-20">
      <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-extrabold mb-6">
        Our Emergency Tree Removal Response Process
      </h2>
      <p class="text-lg text-white/90 leading-relaxed">
        When a tree emergency occurs, fast and organized action is critical.
        Our emergency tree removal process is designed to secure your property,
        eliminate hazards, and restore safety as quickly as possible.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- STEPS -->
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-10">

      <!-- STEP 1 -->
      <div class="bg-white/95 text-slate-900 rounded-3xl p-8">
        <span class="block text-sm font-bold text-teal-700 mb-4">
          STEP 1
        </span>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-extrabold mb-4">
          Immediate Emergency Assessment
        </h3>
        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
          Our emergency response team arrives quickly to assess storm damage,
          fallen trees, and hazardous conditions. We identify immediate risks to
          people, structures, vehicles, and power lines.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- STEP 2 -->
      <div class="bg-white/95 text-slate-900 rounded-3xl p-8">
        <span class="block text-sm font-bold text-teal-700 mb-4">
          STEP 2
        </span>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-extrabold mb-4">
          Site Securing & Safety Measures
        </h3>
        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
          Before removal begins, we secure the area using professional safety
          protocols. This includes stabilizing trees, controlling access, and
          preparing equipment to prevent further damage or injury.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- STEP 3 -->
      <div class="bg-white/95 text-slate-900 rounded-3xl p-8">
        <span class="block text-sm font-bold text-teal-700 mb-4">
          STEP 3
        </span>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-extrabold mb-4">
          Controlled Emergency Tree Removal
        </h3>
        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
          Using cranes, lifts, and precision cutting techniques, our crew
          performs controlled tree removal. Debris is cleared efficiently to
          restore safe access to your property.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>

    <!-- BOTTOM LINE -->
    <div class="mt-20 text-center">
      <p class="text-white/90 text-lg">
        Available 24/7 for emergency tree removal across South Florida.
      </p>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>

<!-- ================= EMERGENCY SERVICE AREA ================= -->
<section class="bg-[#f4f8f6] py-32">
  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6">

    <!-- HEADER -->
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto text-center mb-16">
      <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 mb-6">
        Emergency Tree Removal Across South Florida
      </h2>

      <p class="text-lg text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
        Our emergency tree removal teams are available 24/7 throughout South
        Florida, providing rapid response for storm damage, fallen trees, and
        hazardous situations that require immediate professional action.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- CONTENT -->
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto space-y-8 text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">

      <p>
        We proudly serve homeowners, businesses, and property managers across
        <strong class="text-slate-900">Miami</strong>,
        <strong class="text-slate-900">Fort Lauderdale</strong>,
        <strong class="text-slate-900">Broward County</strong>, and surrounding
        South Florida communities. Our local emergency crews understand the
        unique risks caused by hurricanes, tropical storms, heavy rainfall, and
        high winds common to this region.
      </p>

      <p>
        Because tree emergencies often occur outside normal business hours, our
        teams remain on standby day and night. Whether a tree has fallen across
        a driveway, damaged a roof, blocked a roadway, or become entangled with
        power lines, we respond quickly to restore safety and access.
      </p>

      <p>
        With strategically positioned crews and professional equipment, we are
        able to provide <strong class="text-slate-900">fast emergency tree
        removal services</strong> throughout South Florida without delays. Our
        priority is to secure the site, prevent further damage, and complete
        controlled tree removal as efficiently as possible.
      </p>

    </div>

    <!-- CTA -->
    <div class="mt-20 text-center">
      <a
        href="/contact-us/"
        class="inline-flex items-center gap-4 rounded-full
               bg-teal-700 px-12 py-5 text-white font-extrabold
               hover:bg-teal-800 transition"
      >
        Request Emergency Service
        <span class="flex h-10 w-10 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-white/15">
          ↗
        </span>
      </a>

      <p class="mt-6 text-sm text-slate-500">
        24/7 emergency response across Miami, Fort Lauderdale & Broward County
      </p>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>

<!-- ================= EMERGENCY TREE REMOVAL FAQ ================= -->
<section class="bg-white py-28">
  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6">

    <!-- HEADER -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto text-center mb-16">
      <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 mb-4">
        Emergency Tree Removal FAQs
      </h2>
      <p class="text-lg text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
        Below are answers to the most common questions about emergency tree
        removal services in South Florida. If you are facing a tree emergency,
        our team is available 24/7 for immediate assistance.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- FAQ LIST -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto divide-y divide-slate-200">

      <!-- FAQ ITEM -->
      <div class="py-6">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-extrabold text-slate-900 mb-2">
          What is considered an emergency tree removal?
        </h3>
        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
          Emergency tree removal is required when a tree poses an immediate risk
          to people, property, or infrastructure. This includes storm-damaged or
          fallen trees, trees leaning toward structures, broken limbs hanging
          overhead, and trees entangled with power lines.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- FAQ ITEM -->
      <div class="py-6">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-extrabold text-slate-900 mb-2">
          Do you provide 24/7 emergency tree removal services?
        </h3>
        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
          Yes. We provide 24/7 emergency tree removal services across South
          Florida, including nights, weekends, and holidays. Our emergency crews
          are on standby to respond quickly to urgent situations.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- FAQ ITEM -->
      <div class="py-6">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-extrabold text-slate-900 mb-2">
          How fast can your emergency tree removal team respond?
        </h3>
        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
          Response times depend on location and severity, but our goal is to
          dispatch an emergency tree removal crew as quickly as possible. With
          teams positioned throughout South Florida, we are able to provide
          rapid response to storm damage and hazardous tree situations.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- FAQ ITEM -->
      <div class="py-6">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-extrabold text-slate-900 mb-2">
          Can you remove trees that are on or near power lines?
        </h3>
        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
          Yes. Trees entangled with power lines require controlled, professional
          emergency tree removal using specialized equipment and strict safety
          protocols. These situations should never be handled without trained,
          licensed professionals.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- FAQ ITEM -->
      <div class="py-6">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-extrabold text-slate-900 mb-2">
          Is emergency tree removal more expensive?
        </h3>
        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
          Emergency tree removal costs vary depending on tree size, location,
          accessibility, and the complexity of the situation. While emergency
          jobs may involve additional resources, we provide transparent pricing
          and clear estimates before work begins whenever possible.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- FAQ ITEM -->
      <div class="py-6">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-extrabold text-slate-900 mb-2">
          Do I need a permit for emergency tree removal?
        </h3>
        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
          Permit requirements vary by city and county in South Florida. In many
          emergency situations, immediate removal is allowed to prevent further
          damage or danger. Our team can assist with local regulations and any
          required documentation.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- FAQ ITEM -->
      <div class="py-6">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-extrabold text-slate-900 mb-2">
          What happens after the emergency tree is removed?
        </h3>
        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
          After emergency tree removal, our crew performs complete cleanup,
          including debris removal and clearing access to your property.
          Additional services such as stump grinding or follow-up tree care can
          be arranged if needed.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- FAQ ITEM -->
      <div class="py-6">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-extrabold text-slate-900 mb-2">
          Are your emergency tree removal services licensed and insured?
        </h3>
        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
          Yes. SF Tree Removal is fully licensed and insured, ensuring that every
          emergency tree removal project meets professional safety, liability,
          and quality standards.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>

    <!-- CTA -->
    <div class="mt-14 text-center">
      <a
        href="/contact-us/"
        class="inline-flex items-center gap-3 rounded-full
               bg-teal-700 px-10 py-4 text-white font-extrabold
               hover:bg-teal-800 transition"
      >
        Request Emergency Service
        <span class="flex h-8 w-8 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-white/15">
          ↗
        </span>
      </a>

      <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-slate-500">
        24/7 emergency response across South Florida
      </p>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>

<!-- ================= FINAL EMERGENCY CTA ================= -->
<section class="relative bg-teal-900 py-32 text-white overflow-hidden">
  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 text-center">

    <!-- URGENCY BADGE -->
    <span
      class="inline-block mb-8 px-4 py-1 text-xs font-bold tracking-widest
             border border-dashed border-white/60 rounded-full"
    >
      24/7 EMERGENCY TREE REMOVAL
    </span>

    <!-- HEADLINE -->
    <h2 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl xl:text-6xl font-extrabold leading-tight">
      Tree Emergency?
      <br class="hidden sm:block" />
      Request Immediate Assistance
    </h2>

    <!-- SUPPORTING LINE -->
    <p class="mt-8 max-w-3xl mx-auto text-lg text-white/90">
      Fallen trees, storm damage, or hazardous situations require fast,
      professional action. Our emergency tree removal crews are available
      around the clock across South Florida.
    </p>

    <!-- PRIMARY ACTION -->
    <div class="mt-14">
      <a
        href="/contact-us/"
        class="inline-flex items-center gap-4 rounded-full
               bg-white px-14 py-6 text-teal-900 text-lg font-extrabold
               hover:bg-slate-100 transition"
      >
        Request a Free Estimate
        <span
          class="flex h-10 w-10 items-center justify-center rounded-full
                 bg-teal-900 text-white"
        >
          ↗
        </span>
      </a>
    </div>

    <!-- TRUST LINE -->
    <p class="mt-10 text-sm text-white/70">
      Licensed & insured · Rapid emergency response · Serving all of South Florida
    </p>

  </div>
</section>

</BaseLayout>
